<h2>The timeline that decided the case</h2>
<div class="flow">
<div class="fstep"><strong>2019</strong> — marriage; discord follows within a year, and the wife institutes a dowry-cruelty case at Patna (Beur P.S. Case No. 135 of 2020).</div>
<div class="fstep"><strong>September 2022</strong> — the Judicial Magistrate takes cognizance against the husband, the chargesheet having named him alone.</div>
<div class="fstep"><strong>July 2023</strong> — the parties file a joint compromise petition in the Family Court; the wife records receipt of final alimony and the absence of any remaining claim.</div>
<div class="fstep"><strong>September 2023</strong> — the Family Court, Patna decrees divorce by mutual consent under Section 13-B of the Hindu Marriage Act.</div>
<div class="fstep"><strong>October 2026</strong> — the High Court quashes the cognizance order and all consequential proceedings.</div>
